Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:45:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/34] flashnext cuda: fn_qsa_select keeps 8 keys in flight a
 pass and places its picks by warp runs

Upstream TensorFold commit by Armin, ported onto this series (see the note below for its upstream source).

Part of upstream 2a92fb6c9 (#1764): the sparse-index select's radix passes load 8 keys a thread before
their histogram adds (one L2 wait a key was the pass's time), one warp finds each pass's cut, and the picks
are placed by warp runs with ballots and two block scans. The same ids, ties included, in the same order.
fn_qsa_select_lanes shares the body, so a shared decode or verify round's select takes it too.

(cherry picked from commit 2a92fb6c9e87bad0053117ba2e008dde2ba5761b, fn_qsa_select hunks only)
